{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sporting-feudalist-bluet","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nIn run 44232977541 at dd72b461814, the \"sweep (windows)\" job (134562252974) failed `tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py::test_concurrent_cursor_writes_never_report_a_write_error`:\n\n`AssertionError: a concurrent cursor write was silently dropped: ['reconcile_cursor_write_error']` (`tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py:182`)\n\nThe test races 2 threads through `rebar.review_bot.reconcile._write_cursor`, with a barrier on the replace step. The same test did not fail in the Windows sweeps of runs 44211859981 (fc446d89df7) or 44141097601 (83ca81e709e).\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- Windows `os.replace` raises `PermissionError` when the target is held open, or is being replaced concurrently, by the other writer. POSIX rename semantics allow that.\n- An intermittent race that the earlier runs did not hit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The failing OSError (type and winerror) is captured from a Windows run, with the test's emitted event kwargs recorded.\n- [ ] Concurrent cursor writes on Windows never emit `reconcile_cursor_write_error`, with the cause fixed at class level.","id":"f59a-4c53-9452-4d3f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: concurrent review-bot cursor writes emit reconcile_cursor_write_error"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794978494543551164,"uuid":"f9c51bc0-8adf-4dc4-b349-210aea4e1668"}